    "commit": "d56448c7e10251b217d973e037352675f5874980",
    "changes": [
      "The default minimal admission predicate rejects an oversized public length with a widened comparison before accepting the fixed-shape fast path.",
      "ArchiveInfo::new and MessageInfo::new are inlineable, and fixed message versions are copied with one extend operation.",
      "Public mutation checks and strict-profile admission remain on their existing paths; no unchecked provenance is introduced.",
      "Retained-header comparison now uses target-derived lengths only while the current projection still matches; after divergence it emits the current payload and recalculates the length prefix.",
      "A direct packed-field cardinality mutation regression proves canonical fallback preserves the changed public metadata and exact re-encoding."
    ],
